The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```
if (ib_copy_to_udata(udata, &srq->msrq.srqn, sizeof (__u32))) {
    err = -EFAULT;
    goto err_wrid;
}
```
Reason:
After a successful `mlx4_srq_alloc()`, if `ib_copy_to_udata()` fails, the error path jumps to `err_wrid` which does not call `mlx4_srq_free()`, resulting in a resource leak of the allocated SRQ.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```
if (ib_copy_to_udata(udata, &srq->msrq.srqn, sizeof (__u32))) {
    err = -EFAULT;
    goto err_srq;
}
...
err_srq:
    mlx4_srq_free(dev->dev, &srq->msrq);
```
Reason:
By adding a new label `err_srq` that calls `mlx4_srq_free()` before falling through to `err_wrid`, the SRQ resource is properly freed when the copy to user space fails, preventing the leak.

